From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] meson: phoenix backend -- the optional fcntl()/dup()
 interposers

phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_fcntl.c and phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_dup.c keep
a duplicated in-process sync file a sync file for programs linked with
-Wl,--wrap=fcntl -Wl,--wrap=dup -Wl,--wrap=dup2 (Mesa duplicates every
EGL native fence with fcntl(F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC) before importing it). Their
own archive members, like drm_phoenix_wrap_ioctl.c: a program linked
without those flags never pulls them.
---
 meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@ if host_machine.system() == 'phoenix'
     'phoenix/drm_phoenix_v3d.c', 'phoenix/drm_phoenix_logic.c',
     'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap.c',
     'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_ioctl.c',
+    'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_fcntl.c', 'phoenix/drm_phoenix_wrap_dup.c',
   )
   inc_phoenix = [include_directories('phoenix')]
 endif
